gosh seam 11: What a program puts on the clipboard is passed on each time, with its selection.

For:   REQ20/TERM-1 (gosh#6). Copying in a program on the server, Claude Code among them, often
       did not reach the user's clipboard: upstream passed on OSC 52 only for the selection "c",
       and only when the text differed from the last it passed on.
What:  OSC 52 with any selection (c p q s 0-7, or none) is kept whole after "52;" and sent on as
       the program wrote it; each time text is put on the clipboard is counted, as a bell is, and
       the display sends it when the count changes, not when the text does. So the same text
       twice is sent twice, and a reset no longer sends an empty clipboard. A request to read the
       clipboard ("?") is passed on as before (requirements v20, Not yet answered). Nothing in
       mosh's protocol changes: a stock mosh at the other end does what it did before.
Where: Framebuffer (terminalframebuffer.h, .cc): clipboard_count beside bell_count;
       Dispatcher::OSC_dispatch (terminalfunctions.cc); Display::new_frame (terminaldisplay.cc).
Kind:  adds a field and a helper; one condition widened, one comparison changed. Nothing is moved.
From:  gosh's own, 2026-11-26 (client: "core can be patched", "in seam").
Pin:   upstream mosh at decd9b705eb81626f694335b8d5940538beb06da; cut against the result of the patch before it.

